From 1d0f49b5b029bf27d71ed3b2664a49337fcb8817 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reggie <reggie@moneytracer.dev>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 07:08:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Remove the frost/glassmorphism theming feature and effect
 entirely
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- useTheme.jsx: drop FROST_PRESETS, frostKey, customFrostColor,
  frostIntensity, and the --glass-* CSS variable computation, plus the
  now-unused hexToRgbString/rgbStringToHex helpers that only served the
  frost color pickers.
- AppearanceSettings.jsx: remove the Frost Color and Frost Intensity
  controls from the Settings > Appearance panel.
- design-tokens.css / globals.css: delete the --glass-bg/-hover/-border/
  -blur/-saturate/-shadow/-sidebar tokens and every backdrop-filter rule
  that used them (sidebar, cards, modals, login card, pill nav, etc.),
  replacing translucent glass backgrounds with solid --surface/
  --surface-sunken and --border/--border-strong.
- Accordion.jsx, Reports.jsx: swap remaining --glass-bg/-hover usages for
  solid surface tokens.
- Landing.jsx: strip its own inline backdrop-filter/blur declarations.
- Cleaned up stale 'frosted glass' comments in globals.css/Settings.jsx.

Left untouched: the decorative ambient background blobs (.app-blob,
.login-orb-*) and the unrelated blur() on the unsaved-changes modal
scrim — neither is the frosted-glass panel effect itself.
